1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:07,562
Grandmother said an emperor camped under
Mount Tossa saw a comet, and named the

2
00:00:07,562 --> 00:00:09,490
place Dessie: my joy.

3
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:18,430
At seven, I made a comet of my own:
old socks, plastic bags and string.

4
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:26,120
Nothing in Dessie is flat. Even our
football pitch climbed the mountain.

5
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:34,677
Our rule: kick it in the ditch, you
climb in after it. Hayat's left foot is

6
00:00:34,677 --> 00:00:37,430
the reason that rule exists.

7
00:00:38,192 --> 00:00:48,402
Four–four. Next goal wins. Then the fog
came down from Tossa like a white gabi.

8
00:00:49,192 --> 00:00:55,937
I couldn't see anything but my comet. I
kicked it with all I had. It vanished

9
00:00:55,937 --> 00:00:59,132
into the fog. “GOAL!” shouted Dawit.

10
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:07,829
Grandmother laughed and pulled me under
her gabi: “A comet doesn't stay. It only

11
00:01:07,829 --> 00:01:10,740
shows you where your joy is.”

12
00:01:11,525 --> 00:01:17,767
Today, when people ask where I'm from, I
say Dessie. And then I tell them what it

13
00:01:17,767 --> 00:01:18,235
means.
